<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ptolemaic Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ptolemaic dynasty, Ptolemaic Empire, Ptolemaic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ptolemaic Kingdom was a Hellenistic state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> founded in 305 BCE by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I Soter</a>, one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>'s generals, after the break-up of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>. Ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>, it combined Greek administration with pharaonic tradition. A long-standing rival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>, it ended with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii">Cleopatra VII</a> and Roman annexation in 30 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom.jpg" alt="Ptolemaic Kingdom" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ptolemaic Kingdom III-II century BC - ru.svg: Kaidor (talk · contribs) derivative work: rowanwindwhistler (talk) deri... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemaic_Kingdom_III-II_century_BC_-_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
